# Vulnerabilities knowingly accepted in the CI image scan (.github/workflows/ci.yml).
# Every entry carries its reason and an expiry date: once it expires, Trivy reports it again and CI fails, so nothing
# stays ignored forever. When the fix ships, remove the entry and update the image.

# golang.org/x/net 0.60.0 compiled into /usr/bin/caddy (caddy:2.11.9-alpine, the latest release).
# The fix (x/net 0.62.0) is not in any Caddy release yet; rebuilding Caddy with xcaddy just for this adds maintenance
# that does not pay off. Review with the next Caddy release (Dependabot proposes it).
CVE-2026-78661 exp:2026-12-31

# libpam 1.5.2-6+deb12u2 in the builder image, from node:22.23.5-slim (Debian 12). Checked 2026-11-27: that pinned
# digest is still the latest node:22-slim, and node:22-trixie-slim (Debian 13) trades it for another fixable HIGH
# (libzstd1), so no node:22 image has the fix (deb12u3) yet. The flaw is in pam_namespace, which needs a PAM login:
# the builder runs `node` as uid 1000 with no login, su or sshd, no capabilities and no-new-privileges. Remove it with
# the first node:22-slim digest that ships deb12u3 (Dependabot proposes it).
CVE-2025-6020 exp:2027-01-26
